        <key>boundary</key>
        <string>Two-cut prototype for encoded U1D7B. No ordinary I alias, unchanged-glyph self-substitution or empty-uppercase feature exemption. All-cut roles, actual inheritance/kerning and target-size repeated/adjacent spacing remain separate.</string>
        <key>construction</key>
        <string>Keep the entire genuine same-cut SC I stem. Extract the complete native U1D7B crossbar between its actual two interior levels and translate it without scaling to the genuine SC shaft. Add equal shaft length above/below that native bar, preserving its optical offset above halfway. Preserve the defining phonetic glyph outer-bar bearing roles, including their negative values, rather than adding ordinary I stem bearings outside both arms.</string>
        <key>kerningBoundary</key>
        <string>The ordinary SC bodies are construction controls, not automatic new-glyph edge-kerning aliases. Preserve the stated actual outer-bearing policy and measure both edges/adjacent contexts; no forced correction cancels the reflected branch or defining crossbar.</string>
